// A PARTIAL pin: `callerPrincipal = principal` is pinned on `request` but
// NOT on `response`. Per the universality requirement, a pin declared on
// only some event kinds is NOT universal, so it must NOT activate key-local
// (partition) semantics — the leaf keeps GLOBAL-trace semantics, silently and
// with no error. This is the safety direction of the partition guarantee: the
// engine must not grant isolation the schema did not earn.
//
// This bundle is the deliberate inverse of 1155 (same policy, same trace) whose
// schema pins `callerPrincipal` on BOTH kinds (universal → partition active).
// 1155 PERMITS its trace (the foreign event is excluded); this bundle must
// DENY the same trace (the foreign event is the global `previous` and is NOT
// excluded). A bug that treated this partial pin as universal would wrongly
// make this bundle's verdict match 1155's.

decision event <A>::request {
    ...inputs(A),
    pin callerPrincipal: principalType(A) = principal,
    callerResource:  resourceType(A),
    requestId:       String,
}

event <A>::response {
    ...inputs(A),
    ...outputs(A),
    callerPrincipal: principalType(A),
    callerResource:  resourceType(A),
    requestId:       String,
}
